Subject: (cherry-pick-branch-heads/8103) [M157] ApplyEncoderSwitch() must not
 modify negotiated codecs list.

Original change's description:
> ApplyEncoderSwitch() must not modify negotiated codecs list.
>
> Modifying the negotiated list was an easy way to keep track of which
> codecs remain that have not been attempted yet. Unfortunately, this
> causes setParameters() to fail when the application is asking to
> reconfigure the same codec again (which is perfectly valid to try since
> it is still negotiated). The app should be allowed to try again and a
> simple get+setParameters() that doesn't change anything should never
> fail.
>
> The fix is to introduce `available_negotiated_codecs_`, which is
> simply a copy of `negotiated_codecs_` that ApplyEncoderSwitch() is
> able to modify.
>
